      "content": "but \"influenced by political motives\" is a pretty heavy way to put it. if the memos clearly show he was misrepresenting what he saw in the briefing, isn't it more accurate to say he was being intentionally deceptive to push a specific agenda? it feels like there's a difference between just being inconsistent and actually lying for political gain. shouldn't we call that what it is?",
