      "content": "but the memos are already released and they're right there in the public record. the discrepancy isn't a \"maybe,\" it's an actual conflict between his words and the documents. at this stage, treat it like a legal analysis—if a witness says X and a document says Y, and they should have known about the document, isn't it more intellectually honest to conclude that the testimony was a bad-faith attempt to manipulate the hearing? why do we need to wait for \"more evidence\" of an agenda when the deception itself is already visible?",
